MusicHud-TuneWeave audio codec module

The original authors' decoder sources, copyrights and license texts are retained
under vendor/upstream and META-INF/licenses/audio-codecs in the shaded artifact.
Source identities and local patches are recorded in vendor/manifest.json.

JLayer: JavaLayer authors, LGPL; unchanged decoder core.
JOrbis/Jogg: JCraft and original authors, GNU Library GPL; three local patches
correct multichannel indexing and bound untrusted setup allocations.
Concentus: Logan Stromberg and the Opus authors, BSD terms; unchanged sources.
ALAC: Peter McQuillan / David Hammerton, BSD terms; finite20-bit packing and sign-extension patch.
WavPack Tiny Decoder: David Bryant / Peter McQuillan, BSD terms; finite float intermediate-preservation hook, unchanged prediction/entropy algorithms.
AAC: JAAD / Vavi authors, retained upstream public-domain dedication; finite compatibility/correctness patches and four read-only access-unit recovery
observers plus two configuration-state getters, with originals and complete diffs. Recovery observation does not copy
DSP/filter state or alter decoding arithmetic.
The separate TNS filtering overlay adapts FFmpeg n9.0.2 apply_tns and the
unnormalized compute_lpc_coefs recursion, LGPL 2.1 or later: copyright
2005-2006 Oded Shimon, 2006-2007 Maxim Gavrilov, 2008-2013 Alex Converse,
2006 Justin Ruggles. It uses the project LGPL text and preserves the public-domain
JAAD parser. Reference: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n9.0.2/libavcodec


The separate AAC Main prediction overlay corrects per-channel predictor history,
common-window syntax copying, short-window resets and reset-group validation.
State/reset behavior was checked against FFmpeg n9.0.2 aacdec_dsp_template.c and
AAC float prediction code, LGPL 2.1 or later: copyright 2005-2006 Oded Shimon,
2006-2007 Maxim Gavrilov, 2008-2013 Alex Converse. The original JAAD code retains
its public-domain dedication. Reference: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n9.0.2/libavcodec/aac

The separate WavPack integer precision adapter follows the scalar supplemental
bit/CRC arithmetic of FFmpeg 9.0.2, LGPL-2.1-or-later. Its corresponding notice
and license are retained alongside the adapter source. This module does not
embed FFmpeg native code or JNI binaries.

Local adapters and integration are part of MusicHud-TuneWeave under its existing
LGPL license. The project source distribution includes corresponding third-party
sources, finite patches and upstream attribution; preserve these on redistribution.

WMA1/2: isolated FFmpeg-derived Java core from pinned devoxin source, LGPL2.1+,
finite sign/overlap/input-boundary corrections; no Lavaplayer dependency/JAR.
APE: controlled FFmpeg9.0.2 scalar Java translation, LGPL2.1+; original C
references and finite namespace integration diffs are retained with the source.
AIFF/AIFC/AU: project-owned bounded PCM container reader, no third-party DSP.

The SBR no-noise-envelope gain compensation overlay is checked against FFmpeg
n9.0.2 aacsbr.c, LGPL-2.1-or-later, retaining its author attribution in source.
